{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdMeromorphic","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdMeromorphic","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.PhiBProd","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Meromorphic.Divisor"],"declarations":1,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdMeromorphic.phiBProd_meromorphicOn_of_analytic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdMeromorphic.phiBProd_meromorphicOn_of_analytic","kind":"theorem","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/PhiBProdMeromorphic.lean#L40-L55","doc":"**`phiBProd` is meromorphic on `ℂ` given analyticity of its two products.**\n`phiBProd b = num / den` with `num z = ∏' k, numFactor b z k`,\n`den z = ∏' k, denFactor b z k`; an analytic-÷-analytic quotient is meromorphic. This\ndischarges the `MeromorphicOn` input of the divisor-route brick (c) for the concrete\n`Φ_b`, leaving only `AnalyticOnNhd` of the products (the infinite-product-analyticity\ninput) open. ","signatureChunk":0}]}